course: dictionary
lesson: 475
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. Arsenal is one of them. The clues in the sentence tell you which meaning is right. «The Arsenal of Venice was a huge state shipyard» describes a place where ships were built, not a football club.
explain: Read the words around the word. Words like «nuclear» or «weapons» point to a store of weapons. Words like «fan» or «club» point to the football team. Then ask: which meaning fits this sentence?
explain: The second meaning is a figure of speech. «An arsenal of jokes» means a big set of jokes you can use, like a box full of tools. In Ollie's story, «My dad plays for Arsenal, swear down» means he is claiming a famous link to the football club. "Swear down" is British slang for "I promise".
explain: Capital letters help too. Arsenal with a capital A is a name, usually the football club in north London, nicknamed the Gunners. Lowercase arsenal is a common word for a store of weapons, or a big set of tools, tricks or ideas.
fact: An arsenal is a big collection of weapons, or a building where weapons are made or stored.
fact: An arsenal can also be any big set of tools, tricks or ideas: «an arsenal of jokes» means many jokes ready to use.
fact: Arsenal with a capital letter is a famous football club in north London, England, nicknamed «the Gunners».
fact: «Nuclear arsenal» means a country's collection of nuclear weapons.
fact: «The Arsenal of Venice» was a huge state workplace where ships were built one after another, almost like a factory.
exercise: «The country has a nuclear arsenal.» What does arsenal mean here? | A small garden shed | A football team | *A big collection of weapons | A set of jokes
exercise: «She has an arsenal of skills for the game.» What does arsenal mean here? | A cold, empty room | A football club in London | A place where ships are built | *A big set of tricks and skills, ready to use
exercise: Jake says, «I support Arsenal, the Gunners.» Which meaning of Arsenal is this? | A big collection of weapons | A workplace where ships were built | *The football club in north London | A set of jokes
test: «The Arsenal of Venice built ships one after another, almost like a factory.» What kind of place was it? | *A huge state workplace where ships were built | A football ground | A quiet park by the sea | A shop selling jokes
test: In Ollie's story, why does nobody believe him? | Because he is the best player in the class | *Because his dad does not play for Arsenal, so it was a lie | Because he always tells the truth | Because he has a new puppy
exam: Which sentence uses arsenal to mean a big set of tools, tricks or ideas? | The Arsenal game was on TV last night | Jo kicked the ball past the goalie | The army kept its arsenal in an old fort | *She has an arsenal of ideas for the school project
